Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoders and encoders are original implementations written from the
formats' public specifications: GIF89a (CompuServe, 1990), Microsoft's
documentation of the BMP/DIB file format (BITMAPFILEHEADER,
BITMAPCOREHEADER, BITMAPINFOHEADER, BITMAPV4HEADER, BITMAPV5HEADER, the
RLE4/RLE8 encodings and BI_BITFIELDS), IBM's OS/2 bitmap headers, TIFF
Revision 6.0 (Adobe, 1992) with the Adobe TIFF Technical Notes, ITU-T T.4
and T.6 (fax coding). They are not
translations of, and do not derive from, any other implementation's source
(image-rs, giflib, libtiff, zlib, stb and others were not read).
DEFLATE for TIFF comes from rivet-png, rivet's PNG crate, written the same
way from RFC 1950 and RFC 1951. docs/PROVENANCE.md records each source and
how the tables were verified.

The codecs are checked against public test corpora — Jason Summers' BMP
Suite, libtiff's sample and test images, and Robert Ancell's GIF test
suite — used as data, fetched by tools/fetch_corpora.py and not distributed
here.

